 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`. I ran one check, parsing a program with a `DEFFRAME` that sets `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-7`. The attribute appeared on the resulting `DefFrame` and printed back out as `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-07`. I didn't run the test suite or add tests.\n\nThe changes are:\n- **Grammar:** `pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark` accepts `CHANNEL-DELAY` as a frame attribute.\n- **Parser:** `pyquil/_parser/parser.py` maps it to a new `channel_delay` field.\n- **`DefFrame`:** `pyquil/quilbase.py` gets an optional `channel_delay` float, so you can construct a `DefFrame` with it, and `out()` includes it when set.\n\nI didn't add `CHANNEL-DELAY` to the reserved-word list in `quilbase.py` (the one that includes `INITIAL-FREQUENCY` and `SAMPLE-RATE`). `CENTER-FREQUENCY` and `ENABLE-RAW-CAPTURE` aren't in that list either, so I left it alone.",
